  <!-- Tooltips -->
  <s:String x:Key="H_Name">Unique identifier, used as the correlation key in logs and as the working directory name. Changing it creates a new configuration: the previous one remains until deleted.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="H_Template">Name of a declared template. The configuration inherits every value from it and only overrides its own differences. Across dozens of mailboxes sharing one tenant, a configuration comes down to three lines.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="H_InitialLookback">Applies to the very first cycle only, when nothing has been processed yet for this mailbox. Too low a value makes it look like nothing is arriving while the service works fine, and nothing reports it.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="H_NotBefore">No message older than this date will ever be processed. Set it at go-live when history is not being imported: without it, the first run processes everything sitting in the mailbox.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="H_Timeout">Once exceeded, the converter is KILLED rather than waited for. A LibreOffice instance stuck on a corrupt document never recovers: without this timeout, one document freezes a conversion slot for good.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="H_OnFailure">Substitute produces a page carrying the file name and the reason, so the ECM sees something is missing. Skip drops the part silently. RejectMessage rejects the whole message.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="H_Naming">Tokens: {date} {time} {received} {guid} {mailbox} {config} {subject} {from} {index} {name} {ext} {node}. A format may follow a colon. In PerAttachment mode, {index} is mandatory or files overwrite each other.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="H_AtomicWrite">The file is written under a temporary extension, then renamed. Without it, an ECM watching the folder can pick up a PDF mid-write, and the error is undetectable on its side.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="H_AllOrNothing">If one target fails, deliveries already made to the others are rolled back. An ECM holding a message that another one never received creates a reconciliation gap nobody notices before the audit.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="H_AcceptAnyCertificate">Removes every protection against interception: a third party can sit between the service and the server undetected. Enable only against a known self-signed certificate, and document it.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="H_HonorRetryAfter">Graph states how long to wait after throttling. Ignoring it makes things worse: the service resumes at once, gets throttled again, and the quota recovers more and more slowly.</s:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
